KERNEL IO ERROR SCAN
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Commands:

# SCSI/ATA/NVMe errors in last 2 weeks
  journalctl -k --since "2 weeks ago" --no-pager | \
    grep -iE 'ata[0-9]|scsi|nvme|blk_update|i/o error|medium error|
              sense key|buffer i/o|end_request|reset|link down|timeout|
              aborted' | head -50

# Filesystem-level issues
  journalctl -k --since "2 weeks ago" --no-pager | \
    grep -iE 'ext4|xfs|btrfs|zfs|journal_io|remount.*read-only|
              corruption' | head -50

# Task hangs (classic disk-slow indicator)
  journalctl -k --since "2 weeks ago" --no-pager | \
    grep -iE 'blocked for more than|hung_task|task .* blocked|
              khungtaskd|INFO: task' | head -50

Result: All returned empty or non-relevant lines.
Finding: Host kernel IO subsystem is CLEAN:
  - No blocked tasks
  - No IO errors
  - No ATA/NVMe/SCSI errors
  - No filesystem corruption
  - No controller resets

Eliminated: hardware-level IO failure as cause.

