LIVE CAPTURE SCRIPT PROPOSED
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Script for next-spike capture:

  cat > /usr/local/bin/io-snapshot.sh << 'EOF'
  #!/bin/bash
  LOG=/var/log/io-snapshot.log
  while true; do
    {
      echo "=== $(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') ==="
      echo "-- PSI --"
      cat /proc/pressure/io
      cat /proc/pressure/cpu
      cat /proc/pressure/memory
      echo "-- iostat --"
      iostat -xz 1 2 | tail -n +4
      echo "-- top IO processes --"
      ps -eo pid,stat,comm,wchan | awk '$2 ~ /D/'
      echo "-- dirty pages --"
      grep -E 'Dirty|Writeback' /proc/meminfo
      echo ""
    } >> "$LOG"
    sleep 60
  done
  EOF

With systemd service wrapper. Status: not installed.

